body:
Thanks for the contribution. FrozenDictionary provides a faster lookup at the cost of slower creation, and it doesn't seem you have benchmarked this cost. If the dictionary is accessed frequently, it can make sense to use a FrozenDictionary because the faster lookup would outweight the slower startup.

Also, your benchmarks should return the retrieved `Color` to prevent [dead code elimination](https://benchmarkdotnet.org/articles/guides/good-practices.html#avoid-dead-code-elimination).

With this in mind, I modified your benchmarks and run them locally:

```csharp
public class ConstructionBenchmarks {
    [Benchmark(Baseline = true)]
    public Dictionary<string, Color> DictionaryNew() {
        return new Dictionary<string, Color> {
            { "ALICEBLUE", ColorsDictionary.AliceBlue },
            { "ANTIQUEWHITE", ColorsDictionary.AntiqueWhite },
            // [...]
            { "YELLOW", ColorsDictionary.Yellow },
            { "YELLOWGREEN", ColorsDictionary.YellowGreen },
        };
    }
    [Benchmark]
    public FrozenDictionary<string, Color> FrozenDictionaryNew() {
        return new Dictionary<string, Color> {
            { "ALICEBLUE", ColorsDictionary.AliceBlue },
            { "ANTIQUEWHITE", ColorsDictionary.AntiqueWhite },
            // [...]
            { "YELLOW", ColorsDictionary.Yellow },
            { "YELLOWGREEN", ColorsDictionary.YellowGreen },
        }.ToFrozenDictionary();
    }
}
public class LookupBenchmarks {
    [Benchmark(Baseline = true)]
    public Color DictionaryGet() {
        ColorsDictionary.NamedColors.TryGetValue("DARKBLUE", out Color value);
        return value;
    }
    [Benchmark]
    public Color FrozenDictionaryGet() {
        ColorsFrozenDictionary.NamedColors.TryGetValue("DARKBLUE", out Color value);
        return value;
    }
}
```

| Method              | Mean      | Error     | StdDev    | Ratio | RatioSD |
|-------------------- |----------:|----------:|----------:|------:|--------:|
| DictionaryNew       |  3.223 μs | 0.0238 μs | 0.0222 μs |  1.00 |    0.01 |
| FrozenDictionaryNew | 12.798 μs | 0.1190 μs | 0.1113 μs |  3.97 |    0.04 |

| Method              | Mean     | Error     | StdDev    | Ratio |
|-------------------- |---------:|----------:|----------:|------:|
| DictionaryGet       | 7.650 ns | 0.0138 ns | 0.0123 ns |  1.00 |
| FrozenDictionaryGet | 4.918 ns | 0.0222 ns | 0.0208 ns |  0.64 |

As you observed in your benchmark run, lookup is ~1.5 times faster with FrozenDictionary but creation is ~4 times slower.

I'm not sure if the trade-off is worth it, but the extra startup cost is likely negligible in the context of the overall startup time. I'd say it's probably acceptable, so I'm approving, but I'd love to hear others' thoughts.
